<h3>About Me</h3>

<p>
    Hi, my name is Ini.
    <br>
    <br>
    I am an electrical engineering student from Czechia with a strong interest in how hardware and software work.
    <br>
    <br>
    Most of my free time is spent working with Linux, experimenting with programming languages, and building tools
    or small projects that help me better understand technology at a deeper level.<br>I enjoy learning by doing,
    especially when it involves low-level concepts, system design, or clean, well-structured code. That's why i
    mainly code in <a href="https://rust-lang.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rust</a>.
    <br>
    <br>
    I also care a lot about design and usability. I am particularly fond of <a href="https://m3.material.io/"
        target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Material Design 3</a>, and
    colorscheme theory in general.
    <br>
    <br>
    You can find most of my work, along with things I am currently learning or exploring, on my <a
